domain ADR0032:
  description "ADR-0032 revision 1: Separate authoring time boundaries. Status Accepted."
problem P1:
  |
    Decide how focused semantic authoring should contain elapsed time without
    terminating useful work solely because one unsupported wall-clock literal expires.
evidence E1:
  |
    Accepted ADR0031 D7 requires finite elapsed-time containment but D10 and D11 leave
    exact numerical policy to a separately accepted successor decision.
evidence E2:
  |
    Historical D11 design revision two proposed eight calls, 60 seconds per provider
    call and 240 seconds per attempt. Eight worst-case calls require 480 seconds before
    local orchestration, so those maxima do not compose.
evidence E3:
  |
    Current non-normative WIP uses a wall clock beginning at worker execution. It
    terminates at 240 seconds despite semantic progress and terminates the whole run
    after one provider exchange reaches its 60-second reservation.
evidence E4:
  |
    No reviewed evidence establishes representative provider latency percentiles,
    normal focused-call counts, the owner-visible wait budget, or the deployment
    platform deadline for these numerical values.
evidence OWNER_DIRECTION:
  |
    On 2026-09-15, after the behavior and missing authority were presented, the product
    owner identified time-based termination as the main concern and instructed that it
    be corrected.
premise DRIVERS:
  |
    Preserve finite cost and repetition containment, do not confuse transport or worker
    expiry with semantic invalidity, avoid discarding useful progress, and do not select
    a replacement number without workload and platform evidence.
premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Retain the historical literals; remove every time control; or separate provider
    transport timeout, worker execution boundary, semantic no-progress termination and
    cumulative resource ceilings while leaving exact time values pending evidence.
pending U1:
  |
    Provider latency distribution, normal focused call count, owner-visible wait budget,
    hosting deadline, recovery cost and exact replacement values remain undecided.
evidence REVIEW_RESULT:
  |
    Formal review of exact ADR0032 revision one reports PASS with no P0 through P3
    findings and recommends ACCEPT. The review reasoning SHA256 is
    a343bd98f862d7e7f484134ff201ff8c0ae88d8f3590c3af72260426b5ddda6a.
evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-15, immediately after the exact revision one PASS review and its
    complete Japanese scope were presented with ACCEPT or REVISE choices, the
    product owner replied "ACCEPT". The pre-acceptance authoritative SHA256 was
    c9e8ee12edd8f57d796ab389958c8a8f741011fd853b49662f265291bbdb8409.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, OWNER_DIRECTION, DRIVERS, OPTIONS, U1:
  |
    Propose separating four controls. A route-specific provider transport timeout
    bounds one exchange. A worker execution boundary controls one worker lease. Semantic
    no-progress and repeated-state detection determine whether automatic reasoning is
    stalled. Call, step, token and cost ceilings bound cumulative resource consumption.
decision D2 based_on P1, E2, E3, E4, DRIVERS, U1:
  |
    Propose removing a fixed whole-attempt wall-clock expiry as a semantic termination
    condition. Productive progress must not be declared failed solely because a shared
    elapsed-time literal expires. A worker boundary may stop dispatch, fence late
    results and preserve a recoverable technical outcome, but cannot claim semantic
    failure or silently restart consumption.
decision D3 based_on P1, E3, DRIVERS, U1:
  |
    Propose treating provider timeout as a typed transport outcome. It may consume the
    recorded reservation. It does not automatically terminate the entire attempt when
    one explicitly accepted bounded recovery remains within call, token, cost,
    no-progress and fence constraints.
decision D4 based_on P1, E1, E4, OWNER_DIRECTION, U1:
  |
    Keep exact provider and worker time values undecided until the target route and
    platform are named, representative focused requests are measured, an owner-visible
    wait budget is defined, and the product owner accepts the exact policy revision.
    Until then semantic_authoring_policy_v1 is not activation authority.
decision D5 based_on P1, E1, D1, D2, D3, D4:
  |
    If accepted, this ADR refines ADR0031 D7 only for elapsed-time semantics. It retains
    all other ADR0031 boundaries, including finite non-time resource limits, monotonic
    accounting, fenced late-result rejection, focused work, owner review and separate
    rollout authority. It does not authorize implementation, provider calls,
    deployment, route selection or production activation.
decision ACCEPTANCE based_on REVIEW_RESULT, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, D1, D2, D3, D4, D5:
  |
    Accept exact ADR0032 revision one as the time-boundary architecture. Supersede
    ADR0031 as the lifecycle container while retaining all ADR0031 decisions except
    the D7 elapsed-time semantics refined by D1 through D5. This acceptance does not
    select exact time values or authorize design correction, implementation, provider
    calls, deployment, route selection, policy activation, commit or push.
